  "description": "Golden protocol fixtures (T1.03). valid/: schema-valid frames, >=1 per type. invalid/: schema-invalid frames. codec-valid/ and codec-invalid/: schema-valid frames for rules the schema cannot express (UTF-8 byte limits, seq direction, nesting depth, lone surrogates, Feb 29 in non-leap years); the codec accepts codec-valid and rejects codec-invalid. File-name prefix d2s-/s2d- = direction the frame travels. Depth (codec-valid/codec-invalid entries): nesting depth of the open field named in field (skill.call.args, skill.result.output, one skill.manifest.skills[] item), counted as defined in protocol/README.md (Limits and validation notes). Limit (entries with bytes): the max UTF-8 bytes of the field from the README limits table. raw-invalid/: frames whose raw text a strict decoder refuses although a lenient parser reads them; every decoder refuses them. defect repeated-key: schema-valid once a repeated object key is resolved by 'last wins' (also after unescaping, also inside open objects; parsers differ on which duplicate wins). defect not-json: the text is not JSON (an unquoted enum value, a raw control character in a string, NaN/Infinity/1e999/01/+1 or another bare word or a single-quoted value inside an open object); applying repair (replace find by replace) gives a schema-valid frame. Integer fields hold integer literals: invalid/ has the quoted and out-of-range numbers, codec-invalid/ the 1e0 / 2.0 forms (field 'integer').",
